    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48-a2">

                <pb facs="0111" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg77"/>

                <head>Mr. W. Hoffman to the
                        Duke de Gramont.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            17, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I was requested by the ambassador of the North German Confederation, before his
                    departure from Paris, to take the North German subjects residing in French
                    territory under the protection of this legation. To-day I am in receipt of a
                    telegram from my Government authorizing me to do so, provided that it be done
                    with the assent of his Majesty’s government. I have the honor to apply for this
                    assent. * *</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WICKHAM HOFFMAN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Duke de Gramont,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Minister of Foreign Affairs.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
